## frankietemplate.fk — Mustache-compatible template rendering for Frankie
##
## The template engine is implemented in frankie_stdlib.py.
## Stitching this file makes render() and render_file() available.
##
## Usage:
##   stitch "frankietemplate"
##
##   tmpl = "Hello, {{ name }}! You have {{ count }} messages."
##   puts render(tmpl, {name: "Alice", count: 5})
##
##   html = render_file("./views/index.html", {title: "Home"})
##   html_response(html)
##
## Syntax:
##   {{ var }}                          — HTML-escaped interpolation
##   {{{ var }}}                        — raw / unescaped interpolation
##   {{# section }} ... {{/ section }}  — truthy block or vector iteration
##   {{^ inverted }} ... {{/ inverted}} — falsy / empty block
##   {{! comment }}                     — stripped from output

## render(template, data) and render_file(path, data) are built into
## frankie_stdlib.py — no Frankie implementation needed here.
## This file exists so stitch "frankietemplate" signals intent clearly.
